---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Sidebar from '../../components/layout/Sidebar.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<MainLayout title="Gameplay | MCDG" description="Learn the core gameplay loop for MCDG: menus, keybinds, throwing, and multiplayer rounds.">
  <div class="container page-layout">
    <Sidebar />
    <article class="content card">
      <h1>Gameplay</h1>
      <p>MCDG brings disc golf to Minecraft through an in-game menu, calculated disc flight, and multiplayer stroke-play rounds.</p>

      <h2>Opening the Menu</h2>
      <p>Press <kbd>G</kbd> (default) to open the MCDG menu from anywhere. All core actions are available there, so you rarely need to type commands. The keybind can be rebound in <strong>Options → Controls → MCDG</strong>.</p>

      <h2>Keybinds</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Key</th><th>Action</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><kbd>G</kbd></td><td>Open MCDG menu</td></tr>
          <tr><td><kbd>M</kbd></td><td>Add waypoint at current position</td></tr>
          <tr><td><kbd>N</kbd></td><td>Remove nearest waypoint</td></tr>
          <tr><td><kbd>L</kbd></td><td>Toggle waypoint labels</td></tr>
          <tr><td><kbd>+</kbd> / <kbd>-</kbd></td><td>Increase / decrease minimap size</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Admin Flow</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Press <kbd>G</kbd> and choose <strong>Auto Build Course</strong> (or <strong>Manual Build Course</strong> for a seed).</li>
        <li>Enter a course name and confirm placement.</li>
        <li>Open the menu again and go to <strong>Admin → Start Round</strong>.</li>
        <li>Other players can join via <strong>Join Round</strong> in the same menu.</li>
        <li>After each throw, use <strong>Go to Lie</strong> if you ever desync from the marker.</li>
        <li>View scores anytime through <strong>Leaderboard</strong>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Player Flow</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Wait for the admin to start a round, then press <kbd>G</kbd> and choose <strong>Join Round</strong>.</li>
        <li>On your turn, select a disc, stance, and release angle.</li>
        <li>Charge your throw with the power meter, then release.</li>
        <li>Follow the lie marker and throw again until you reach the basket.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Throw Mechanics</h2>
      <p>Disc flight depends on your stance, release angle, disc glide/fade ratings, and wind. See the <a href={`${base}features/physics/`}>physics guide</a> for a deep dive.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Stances:</strong> Overhand, Backhand, Forehand</li>
        <li><strong>Release angles:</strong> Hyzer, Flat, Anhyzer</li>
        <li><strong>Power:</strong> Hold the throw button to charge; overcharging costs stamina.</li>
        <li><strong>Fade:</strong> Discs finish left or right depending on their fade rating and spin.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>For the full tester flow, see the <a href="https://github.com/rbrambley/mcdg/blob/main/USERGUIDE.md">User Guide markdown</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .content {
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .content h1 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
